Nethack does know the day of the week, and the phase of the moon, so it
could calculate Easter, but it would then have to make a religious
decision because different churches have different rules.

There are at least two references to Judaism in the source code, and one
in the game play.  The game has a special rule to get the plural of
"matzoh" correct, should you use that as your fruit name.  The
Candelabrum is called "menorah" in the source code, which is the proper
name for the candelabrum in the Temple in Jerusalem.  That candelabrum
had seven branches, which is why the one in the game needs seven
candles.  ("Menorah" literally refers to any candelabrum, which is why
the nine-branched ones you see on Chanukah have that name, although the
proper Hebrew word is "Chanukiah".)

